*** Keywords ***
Checking No unexpected Active Alarms Raised
    [Arguments]  ${user_unexpected_alarms}=${EMPTY}   ${gnb_index}=0
    [Documentation]   This keyword is used to check no unexpected alarms raised in active alarms list. The unexpeted
    ...    alarms list consists of the default and user defined unexpected alarms.
    ...
    ...    *AUTHOR* calla.wang@nokia-sbell.com
    ...
    ...    |    =Input Parameters=     | =Man.= | =Description= |
    ...    | user_unexpected_alarms | No  | user defined unexpected alarms, it can be a list, or a string, default is empty |
    ...    | gnb_index              | No |  gnb index in testline configurtion file. Default is 0. |
    ...
    ...    ``user_unexpected_alarms`` is like ['10', '34'], '10, 34', '10; 34', '10|34'
    ...
    ...    *RETURN VALUE*
    ...   None
    ...
    ${conn_alias}    generic_utils.get_unique_id_string
    vcu_gen.login_rest   gnb_index=${gnb_index}   alias=${conn_alias}
    ${res}=  vcu_fm_business.no_unexpected_alarms_in_active_alarms   user_unexpected_alarms=${user_unexpected_alarms}
    ...                                                              conn_alias=${conn_alias}
    Should Be True  "${res}"=="${True}"
    [Teardown]    vcu_gen.logout_rest    conn_alias=${conn_alias}

